--
-- CI corpus fixture: 25 real schemes taken from the scraped corpus.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS
--
-- Four e2e tests assert things that only exist when there are schemes to render:
-- verdict cards, the government's own wording behind each one, the expanded
-- ineligible list, and the next-question prompt. CI applies migrations but has
-- no corpus, and the synthetic rows the matching benchmark seeds are deleted
-- again in its afterAll. So those four gates could never run in CI, and did not,
-- from the repository's very first push.
--
-- WHY REAL ROWS RATHER THAN SYNTHETIC ONES
--
-- Invariant 4: every rule keeps the prose it came from. A synthetic fixture
-- would let the source-prose assertion pass against text no government ever
-- wrote, which is precisely what that assertion exists to prevent. These are
-- genuine rows, with genuine prose and genuine myscheme.gov.in URLs.
--
-- COMPOSITION, chosen against the real matcher rather than by eye:
--   For a profile of age 42 in Punjab, 12 of these resolve UNKNOWN and 13 FAIL.
--   The UNKNOWN set produces the visible result cards; the FAIL set produces the
--   "Show N schemes" control. No row PASSes, and that is honest rather than a
--   gap: ~1,100 clauses across the corpus are WILDCARD by design, so PASS is
--   rare, and a fixture that manufactured one would misrepresent the system it
--   is meant to guard.
--
-- REGENERATE with scripts/make-corpus-fixture.sh against a scraped database.
-- Do not hand-edit: each rule tree must stay consistent with the prose beside it.
--

-- This fixture is the entire corpus for the database it loads into.
TRUNCATE schemes;

COPY schemes (id, slug, name, summary, ministry, state, eligibility, source_prose, source_url, benefits, documents, scraped_at, needs_review) FROM stdin;
2c3f6a71-4068-40c5-b8ab-985ee043f48e	aag	{"en": "Aponar Apon Ghar"}	{"en": "\\"Aponar Apon Ghar\\" is a Home Loan Subsidy Scheme by the Finance Department, Govt. of Assam. The objective is to realize the vision of “Housing For All” by 2022 so that each poor person may have their own house. All the applicants will get home loans at subsidized interest rates."}	Finance Department	AS	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["AS"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicants must be permanent residents of Assam state."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "residence", "value": "rural"}, {"op": "lte", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 2000000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The housing loan must be of more than ₹ 5,00,000 and sanctioned by bank on or after 1st April 2019."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The loan accounts must not be under NPA (Non Performing Assets) status."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "This must be the first home by the composite family."}]}	\n1. The applicants must be permanent residents of Assam state.\n1. The applicants must avail the housing loan from any Scheduled Commercial Bank, Regional Rural Banks, Assam Cooperative Apex bank within the state.\n1. The total family income of the applicant (from all sources) must not exceed ₹ 20,00,000.\n1. The housing loan must be of more than ₹ 5,00,000 and sanctioned by bank on or after 1st April 2019.\n1. The loan accounts must not be under NPA (Non Performing Assets) status.\n1. This must be the first home by the composite family.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aag	{"en": "Loan Amount (₹): 5,00,000 - 10,00,000\\nSubsidy (₹): 1,00,000\\n<br>\\n\\nLoan Amount (₹): 10,00,000 - 20,00,000\\nSubsidy (₹): 1,50,000\\n<br>\\n\\nLoan Amount (₹): 20,00,000 - 30,00,000\\nSubsidy (₹): 2,00,000\\n<br>\\n\\nLoan Amount (₹): 30,00,000 - 40,00,000\\nSubsidy (₹): 2,50,000\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:45:13.905+00	t
4b9a6519-6748-478a-bea3-23d265cd0924	aamgsiscs	{"en": "Award of Adhoc Merit Grant (Special Incentive) to Scheduled Caste Students"}	{"en": "The scheme is implemented as a sort of encouragement for the Scheduled Caste students who secure 65% or above marks in matriculation/SSLC Board of Examinations."}	Adi Dravidar Welfare Department, Puducherry	PY	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PY"]}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["sc"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The student should be a permanent resident of the Union Territory of Puducherry by virtue of birth or continuous residence in the Union Territory of Puducherry for not less than five years."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The student should pursue his/her higher studies in a recognized university/college/institution."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The grant will be given irrespective of the income limit of the parent/guardian of the students and the age of the students."}]}	\n   1. All the students belonging to the Scheduled Caste who secured 65% and above marks in the 10th Standard/Matriculation/SSLC Board of Examination shall be eligible for the award.\n   1. The student should be a permanent resident of the Union Territory of Puducherry by virtue of birth or continuous residence in the Union Territory of Puducherry for not less than five years.\n   1. The student should pursue his/her higher studies in a recognized university/college/institution.\n   1. The grant will be given irrespective of the income limit of the parent/guardian of the students and the age of the students.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aamgsiscs	{"en": "\\n   1. Under this scheme, a one-time cash award of ₹1,000/- will be given to the Scheduled Caste students who secure 65% or above marks in matriculation/SSLC Board of Examinations.\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:49:01.788+00	t
f261ee80-9b1d-4949-93c7-3ada8a8b026a	aapd	{"en": "Agricultural Activities for Persons with Disabilities"}	{"en": "This scheme provides loans up to ₹10,00,000/- to the persons with disabilities for agricultural production, irrigation, horticulture, sericulture, the purchase of agricultural machinery and equipment for agricultural services, and the marketing of agricultural products etc."}	Welfare of Scheduled Caste & Backward Classes Department	HR	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["HR"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a permanent resident of Haryana."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have a disability of at least 40%."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be above 18 years old. For persons with mental retardation, the age requirement is relaxed to 14 years instead of the usual 18 years."}]}	\n   1. The applicant should be a permanent resident of Haryana.\n   1. The applicant should have a disability of at least 40%.\n   1. The applicant should be above 18 years old. For persons with mental retardation, the age requirement is relaxed to 14 years instead of the usual 18 years.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aapd	{"en": "\\n   1. Under this scheme, loans up to ₹10,00,000/- are provided to persons with disabilities for agricultural production, irrigation, horticulture, sericulture, purchasing agricultural machinery/equipment for agricultural services, marketing agricultural products, etc.\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:53:44.949+00	t
3602de11-19ee-48f1-b558-5c21e0d18d7d	aas	{"en": "Ashraya Adhar Scheme"}	{"en": "\\"Ashraya Adhar Scheme\\" is introduced to provide financial assistance in the form of loans to the members of Scheduled Tribes for the purpose of repair, renovation/reconstruction of houses. The Goa State Scheduled Tribes Finance and Development Corporation has introduced this scheme."}	Social Welfare Department	GA	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["GA"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "Any person belonging to Scheduled Tribe Community and having his/her house (which shall also include a mundcarial house) either owned individually or jointly will be eligible for financial assistance under this scheme."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "In case the house is owned jointly and there are different family units in the same house residing separately, each such unit will be eligible for financial support."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "The age of the applicant should not be more than 55 years as of the date of the loan application. However, the age of the applicant is relaxed up to 58 years in case the applicant is an employee of the State/ Central Government/ Government Corporation/ Board or aided Institute."}]}	\n1. Any person belonging to Scheduled Tribe Community and having his/her house (which shall also include a mundcarial house) either owned individually or jointly will be eligible for financial assistance under this scheme. \n1. In case the house is owned jointly and there are different family units in the same house residing separately, each such unit will be eligible for financial support.\n1. The age of the applicant should not be more than 55 years as of the date of the loan application. However, the age of the applicant is relaxed up to 58 years in case the applicant is an employee of the State/ Central Government/ Government Corporation/ Board or aided Institute.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aas	{"en": "**₹ 5,00,000/-** advanced as financial assistance in the form of a loan @ 2% per annum. \\n<br>\\n\\n> **Mode of Advance**\\n\\nThe loan amount shall be advanced in two instalments after the submission of the required documents is complete in all respect. \\n**₹ 3,75,000/-** immediately after sanctioning the loan. \\n**₹ 1,25,000/-** on utilization of the first instalment. The 2nd instalment is to be released on submission of utilization bills and on the basis of physical verification/inspection carried out by the officer of the Corporation.\\n<br>\\n\\n**NOTE:** Loanee shall commence the actual work within 03 months from the date of the sanctioned amount released.\\n<br>\\n\\n> **Insurance**\\n\\nThe beneficiary shall be insured for life and property with the Insurance Agency identified by the Corporation and the premium of such policies shall be borne by the loanee (unless and otherwise decided by the Corporation).\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:48:10.945+00	t
5feb2afb-f589-485d-b0c7-43efaeecd7f1	aass	{"en": "Agriculture Academic Studies Scheme"}	{"en": "The objective of the Scheme is to sponsor students for undergoing 4 years of Graduate/degree courses in Agriculture/Horticulture against State quota seats in different Agriculture Universities in the country."}	Agriculture Department	ML	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["ML"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant/student should be a permanent resident of Meghalaya."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Students interested in pursuing a four-year degree course in Agriculture/Horticulture can apply under the scheme."}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["obc"]}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["sc"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should also qualify for the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) All India Entrance Examinations for Admission (AIEEA) conducted by the National Testing Agency (NTA)."}]}	\n   1. The applicant/student should be a permanent resident of Meghalaya.\n   1. Students interested in pursuing a four-year degree course in Agriculture/Horticulture can apply under the scheme.\n   1. The students, general &amp;amp; OBC category, who should have passed 10+2 in the Science stream with 55% aggregate marks having Physics, Chemistry, Biology &amp;amp; English as compulsory subjects are eligible under the scheme.\n   1. The students, SC &amp;amp; ST category, who should have passed 10+2 in the Science stream with 45% aggregate marks having Physics, Chemistry, Biology &amp;amp; English as compulsory subjects are eligible under the scheme.\n   1. The applicant should also qualify for the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) All India Entrance Examinations for Admission (AIEEA) conducted by the National Testing Agency (NTA).\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aass	{"en": "> **Pattern of Assistance:**\\n\\n\\n- Sponsorship of seats, book grants, and scholarships.\\n\\n> **Type of Assistance and Entitlement (If any):**\\n\\n\\n- Monthly stipend @ ₹1,200/-.\\n- Book grant @₹1,200/- per academic year.\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:50:28.143+00	t
39e26de1-91f3-4267-a839-b333d94c1949	abhb	{"en": "Aapki Beti Hamari Beti"}	{"en": "The scheme “Aapki Beti Hamari Beti” was launched by the Department of Women and Child Development, Government of Haryana on 24th August 2015."}	Women and Child Development Department	HR	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["HR"]}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["sc"]}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "eq", "field": "isBPL", "value": true}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "All families whose second girl child is born on or before 21st January 2015, will receive a one-time grant per girl child per annum for five years irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons. **(This is applicable for those cases who are eligible for benefit under the Ladli scheme).**   1. In cases, when twin/multiple girls are born on or before 21st January 2015 will receive a one-time grant per girl child per annum for five years irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons in any family of the State of Haryana satisfying the eligibility conditions. **(This is applicable for those cases who are eligible for benefit under Ladli scheme).**   1. All parents resident of Haryana or having a Haryana domicile and at least one of the parents along with the girl child should be residing in Haryana."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "The pregnant women should be registered at the nearest Anganwadi Centre or with the Health Department."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Beneficiaries should be enrolled in Anganwadi Centre as per their age."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "18 years of age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Unmarried"}]}	The following will be the eligibility criteria for beneficiaries under the scheme:-\n\n   1. All Scheduled Caste families whose first girl child is born on or after 22nd January 2015 shall be eligible to receive a one-time grant.\n   1. All Below Poverty Line (BPL) families whose first girl child is born on or after 22nd January 2015 shall be eligible to receive a one-time grant.\n   1. All families whose second girl child is born on or after 22nd January 2015, will receive a one-time grant irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons.\n   1. In cases, twin/multiple girls born on or after 22nd January 2015, will receive a one-time grant per girl child in any family satisfying the eligibility conditions.\n   1. All families whose second girl child is born on or before 21st January 2015, will receive a one-time grant per girl child per annum for five years irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons. **(This is applicable for those cases who are eligible for benefit under the Ladli scheme).**   1. In cases, when twin/multiple girls are born on or before 21st January 2015 will receive a one-time grant per girl child per annum for five years irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons in any family of the State of Haryana satisfying the eligibility conditions. **(This is applicable for those cases who are eligible for benefit under Ladli scheme).**   1. All parents resident of Haryana or having a Haryana domicile and at least one of the parents along with the girl child should be residing in Haryana.\n   1. The pregnant women should be registered at the nearest Anganwadi Centre or with the Health Department.\n   1. The birth of all girl children shall be registered.\n   1. The girl child shall have an Aadhaar number. However, at the time of enrolment, the Aadhaar number of the parents is also accepted.\n   1. The parents should ensure proper and timely immunization of the girl children and immunization records (as per age of the girl children) should be attached with the application form.\n   1. Beneficiaries should be enrolled in Anganwadi Centre as per their age.\n\n**Change of address:** It shall be obligatory for the parents/guardian of the girl children to intimate any change of address to the Women and Child Development Project Officer/ District Programme Officer and Civil Surgeon concerned.\n**Eligibility to encash Membership Certificate:**\nIn order to obtain the maturity value of the investment in the Membership Certificate at the time of applying the beneficiary girl must be:\n\n- 18 years of age\n- Unmarried\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/abhb	{"en": "**Keeping in view the aims of the Scheme, the Government will provide benefits/financial assistance to each girl child beneficiary. This will be provided in the following manner:**\\n\\n   1. All Scheduled Caste families whose first girl child is born on or after 22nd January 2015 shall be eligible to receive a one-time grant of ₹21,000/- only.\\n   1. All Below Poverty Line (BPL) families whose first girl child is born on or after 22nd January 2015 shall be eligible to receive a one-time grant of ₹21,000/- only.\\n   1. All families whose second girl child is born on or after 22nd January 2015, will receive ₹21000/- (One Time) irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons.\\n   1. In special cases, when twin/multiple girls are born on or after 22nd January 2015 will receive ₹21000/- (One Time) per girl child in any family of the State of Haryana satisfying the eligibility conditions.\\n   1. All families whose second girl child is born on or before 21st January 2015, will receive ₹5000/- girl child per annum for five years irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons. (This is applicable for those cases who were eligible for benefit under the Ladli scheme),\\n   1. In special cases, when twin/multiple girls are born on or before 21st January 2015 will receive ₹2500/- per girl child per annum for five years irrespective of their caste, creed, religion, income, and number of sons in any family of the State of Haryana satisfying the eligibility conditions. (This is applicable for those cases who were eligible for benefit under the Ladli scheme).\\n   1. The money is to be invested with LIC of India under the Scheme &amp;#39;Aapki Beti Harnari Beti&amp;#39; in the name of the girl child beneficiary through her mother. In case, the mother is not alive then the money would be deposited in the name of the beneficiary girl child through the father. If both the parents are not alive then this money would be deposited in the name of the beneficiary girl child through her guardian.\\n\\n**Note:** The money shall be released within one month of submission of the completed application of the beneficiary through her mother/father/guardian.\\n**Withdrawal of Benefit:**\\n\\n   1. The benefit sanctioned under the scheme shall be withdrawn by the competent authority at any stage if it is found that it was sanctioned incorrectly or received by providing false information/fabricated documents.\\n   1. In case of wrong information, deliberately given by the applicant, he/she shall be liable for prosecution as per law.\\n   1. he investment made in the shape of a membership certificate under this scheme shall not be liable for attachment under any law.\\n   1. If the beneficiary dies after attaining the age of 18 years then the parents of the beneficiary will be eligible for receiving benefits.\\n   1. The beneficiary would not be eligible for the benefit under the scheme in case she gets married before the age of 18 years.\\n\\n**Note:** In case of the death of the beneficiary before 18 years of age, her enrolment as a beneficiary under the Scheme Aapki Beti Harnari Beti, would be cancelled with immediate effect, and funds invested against this enrolment would be taken back from Scheme Aapki Beti Hamari Beti with interest and deposited in the receipt Head of the Department.\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:15:52.885+00	t
776c2a42-eb0d-41ef-9834-9d38da7cecb5	abn	{"en": "Anti Bird Net"}	{"en": "Under the Anti Bird Net Birds will never leave your garden if they are used to pecking on certain trees and plants, but if you install anti-bird nets at the appropriate places, you can prevent them from coming again to peck your plants."}	Agriculture Department	RJ	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["RJ"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a native of Rajasthan."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant must have ownership of cultivable land, his own fruit orchard, and an irrigation source."}]}	\n1. The applicant should be a native of Rajasthan.\n1. The applicant must have ownership of cultivable land, his own fruit orchard, and an irrigation source.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/abn	{"en": "> **50 percent subsidy is payable for a maximum area of 5000 square meters.**\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:52:09.529+00	t
2f210b0a-3adc-4e9d-8969-b170d683d398	acaobocwwb	{"en": "Assistance in Case of Accidents (O.B.O.C.W.W.B)"}	{"en": "The “Assistance in Case of Accidents” scheme by the BOCW Welfare Board, Labour Department, Odisha, is a welfare scheme that provides financial assistance to the beneficiary in case of hospitalization and becoming disabled due to an accident.\\n"}	Labour and Employees State Insurance Department	OD	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["OD"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a resident of Odisha."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker."}, {"op": "between", "max": 60, "min": 18, "field": "age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a nominee of a deceased registered member Under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Odisha."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The member should have permanent disability/ lost one limb or eye/ permanent disability without the loss of two limbs or eyes due to an accident."}]}	&gt; **For Registration as a Building/ Construction Worker:**\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a resident of Odisha.\n  - The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker.\n  - The applicant should be between 18 and 60 years.\n  - The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year.\n  - The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law.\n\n&gt; **For the Application of the Welfare Scheme:**\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a nominee of a deceased registered member Under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Odisha.\n  - The member should have permanent disability/ lost one limb or eye/ permanent disability without the loss of two limbs or eyes due to an accident.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/acaobocwwb	{"en": "\\n  - **Permanent total disability due to accident:** ₹1,50,000/-  - **Loss of one limb/ eye:** ₹80,000/-  - **Permanent disability without loss of two limbs/ eyes:** ₹40,000/-\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:55:14.078+00	t
221f6bb2-8352-4737-9362-439fbbf5cf5d	adacw	{"en": "Accidental Death Assistance for the Construction Workers"}	{"en": "\\"Accidental Death Assistance for the Construction Workers\\" by the Delhi Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board, Labour Dept., Delhi, is a welfare scheme that provides financial assistance of ₹2,00,000/- to the nominees/dependents of the members in case the death is due to an accident."}	Labour Department	DL	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["DL"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a resident of Delhi."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Building/Construction Worker."}, {"op": "between", "max": 60, "min": 18, "field": "age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have served the Board for at least 90 days in a given year."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The  nominees/dependents who have lost any registered member/worker of the due to an accidental death."}]}	> **For Registration**\n\n\n- The applicant should be a resident of Delhi.\n- The applicant should be a Building/Construction Worker.\n- The applicant should be between 18 and 60 years.\n- The applicant should have served the Board for at least 90 days in a given year.\n\n<br>\n\n> **For Application**\n\n\n- The  nominees/dependents who have lost any registered member/worker of the due to an accidental death.\n\n<br>\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/adacw	{"en": "\\n- Financial assistance of ₹2,00,000/- is provided to the nominees/dependents of the members in case  the death is due to an accident, during the course of employment.\\n\\n<br>\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:12:02.743+00	t
a33a18f0-0cff-4bc7-b0e8-77fc39c14887	adthsg	{"en": "Adi Dravidar and Tribal Welfare Department-Hostels: Special Guides"}	{"en": "The scheme provides hostel facilities to all boys and girls boarders studying up to XII Standard.\\n"}	Adi Dravidar and Tribal Welfare Department	TN	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["TN"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should be a Student."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should be a resident of Tamil Nadu."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should belong to the Adi Dravidar/ Tribal community."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should be enrolled within XII Standard (Stn. XII or lower)."}]}	\n  - The beneficiary should be a Student.\n  - The beneficiary should be a resident of Tamil Nadu.\n  - The beneficiary should belong to the Adi Dravidar/ Tribal community.\n  - The beneficiary should be enrolled within XII Standard (Stn. XII or lower).\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/adthsg	{"en": "\\n  - **Accommodation:** Hostel facility for all Boys/ Girls Boarders studying upto XII Standard.\\n<br>\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:55:38.409+00	t
67b72228-eaf2-4d72-8857-9b18cb833cab	aes	{"en": "Allowance To Eunuchs Scheme"}	{"en": "The scheme “Allowance to Eunuchs Scheme” was launched by the Department of Social Justice and Empowerment, Government of Haryana on 1st June 2006. Under the scheme, the state government provides financial assistance to eunuchs who are living in various parts of the State."}	Social Justice and Empowerment Department	HR	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["HR"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a permanent resident/domicile of Haryana State and has been residing in Haryana State for the last 5 years at the time of submission of the application."}, {"op": "gte", "field": "age", "value": 18}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant must give a certificate from the Civil Surgeon in support of being an Eunuch."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be involved in any unlawful activity."}]}	\n1. The applicant should be a permanent resident/domicile of Haryana State and has been residing in Haryana State for the last 5 years at the time of submission of the application.\n1. The age of the applicant should not be less than 18 years.\n1. The applicant must give a certificate from the Civil Surgeon in support of being an Eunuch.\n1. The applicant should not be involved in any unlawful activity.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aes	{"en": "1. The financial assistance of ₹2750/- will be given by the state government to eunuchs who are living in various parts of the State.\\n**Note:** If a Eunuch attains the age of 60 years his case will be transferred to Old Age Allowance Scheme.\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:16:45.415+00	t
a05f1fae-d761-4b0b-a2c1-8857f588337f	affr	{"en": "Assistance for Funeral Rites"}	{"en": "The “Assistance for Funeral Rites” scheme provides ₹500/- to support SC/ST families with low income, in covering funeral expenses, ensuring that they can conduct funeral rites for their deceased ones.\\n"}	Adi Dravidar and Tribal Welfare Department	TN	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["TN"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should be a resident of Tamil Nadu."}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["sc", "st"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should have lost any of his/her family members due to death."}]}	\n  - The beneficiary should be a resident of Tamil Nadu.\n  - The beneficiary should belong to the SC/ST (Adi Dravidar/Tribal) community.\n  - The beneficiary should have lost any of his/her family members due to death.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/affr	{"en": "\\n  - **Financial Assistance:** ₹500/- for funeral expenses.\\n&lt;br&gt;\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:56:36.698+00	t
d06cbfb7-8c21-4013-a3e2-202aa88b6961	afpoaa	{"en": "Assistance For Purchase of Aids/Appliances"}	{"en": "The \\"Assistance for Purchase of Aids/Appliances\\" scheme is to provide support to individuals with disabilities by facilitating access to assistive devices and appliances. "}	Social Welfare, Women & Child Development	CH	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["CH"]}, {"op": "lte", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 150000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Applicant must be resident of UT, Chandigarh for more than 3 years."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Applicant&amp;#39;s Disability should be to the extent of 40% and above."}]}	\n   1. Annual income of the applicant from all sources should not exceed  ₹1,50,000/- per annum.\n   1. Applicant must be resident of UT, Chandigarh for more than 3 years.\n   1. Applicant&amp;#39;s Disability should be to the extent of 40% and above.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/afpoaa	{"en": "> **100% cost on purchase of artificial limbs/ aids/ appliances subject to a maximum of ₹40,000/-** \\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:51:03.196+00	t
330cf190-f91c-4a60-a8a5-351118b8cf6d	aktinf	{"en": "Abdul Kalam Technology Innovation National Fellowship"}	{"en": "Indian National Academy of Engineering (INAE) will award \\"Abdul Kalam Technology Innovation National Fellowship\\" to outstanding engineers to recognize, encourage and support translational research by individuals to achieve excellence in engineering, innovation and technology development."}	Ministry Of Science And Technology	\N	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The scheme is applicable to Indian nationals working in India in various capacities of engineering profession in publicly funded institutions."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The scheme is also applicable to Overseas Citizens of India working in permanent positions in publicly funded Institutions in India."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should possess adequate professional qualifications and hold at least a bachelor’s degree with a proven outstanding track record in innovation or technology development."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "This applicant should have a minimum of five (5) years of service left in the parent organization as of the date of the award."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be holding any other fellowship and in the event of selection, he/she will have to opt for only one of the fellowships."}]}	\n   1. The scheme is applicable to Indian nationals working in India in various capacities of engineering profession in publicly funded institutions.\n   1. The scheme is also applicable to Overseas Citizens of India working in permanent positions in publicly funded Institutions in India.\n   1. The applicant should possess adequate professional qualifications and hold at least a bachelor’s degree with a proven outstanding track record in innovation or technology development.\n   1. This applicant should have a minimum of five (5) years of service left in the parent organization as of the date of the award.\n   1. The applicant should not be holding any other fellowship and in the event of selection, he/she will have to opt for only one of the fellowships.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/aktinf	{"en": "\\n   1. The fellowship amount is ₹25,000/- per month in addition to regular income.\\n   1. A Research grant of ₹15.00 lakh per annum.\\n   1. An Overhead of ₹1.00 lakh per annum to the host institute.\\n\\n**Note:** The fellowship is taxable as per the IT rule of the Government of India.\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:48:44.384+00	t
9d7e90aa-a0f5-4b39-a11b-48b4a09c15dd	asd	{"en": "Ashirwad"}	{"en": "The Punjabi government has established the Punjab Ashirwad Scheme to offer financial support for a girl's marriage."}	Department of Social Justice, Empowerment and Minorities	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "lte", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 32790}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The application can be given before the fixed date of marriage or after the 30 days of the marriage by the applicant for getting financial assistance."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["ews"]}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}]}	\n   1. Girl should be 18 years old or above.\n   1. Annual income of the family from all sources does not exceed ₹32,790/-.\n   1. Parents/Guardians of the girl should be domiciled in Punjab State.\n   1. The application can be given before the fixed date of marriage or after the 30 days of the marriage by the applicant for getting financial assistance.\n   1. The amount of Ashirwad is limited up to two girls of the concerned family under the scheme.\n   1. Financial assistance is given to Scheduled Castes/Christian girls, Backward Classes/Castes, Economically weaker sections girls, daughters of widows of any caste at the time of their marriage, and Scheduled Castes widows/divorcees at the time of their re-marriage.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/asd	{"en": "\\n- Financial assistance of ₹51,000/-. \\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:10:09.233+00	t
d6c8236d-b07a-4286-8bc8-e31f2d8cb090	bbgspbocwwb	{"en": "Balri Birth Gift Scheme (P.B.O.C.W.W.B)"}	{"en": "\\"Balri Birth Gift Scheme'' by the BOCW Welfare Board, Dept. of Labour, Punjab, is a welfare scheme that provides financial assistance in the form of a Fixed Deposit Receipt for the birth of a female child (upto two girls per family) which can be encashed only at the time of the daughter's marriage."}	Department of Labour	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a resident of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker (Unorganised Worker)."}, {"op": "between", "max": 60, "min": 18, "field": "age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year."}, {"op": "lt", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 15000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not have membership of the Employees&amp;#39; Provident Fund (EPF)/ National Pension System (NPS)/ Employees&amp;#39; State Insurance Corporation (ESIC)."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be an income tax payer."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a registered member under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have regularly depositing his contribution."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}]}	&gt; ***For Registration as a Building/ Construction Worker:***\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a resident of Punjab.\n  - The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker (Unorganised Worker).\n  - The applicant should be between 18 and 60 years.\n  - The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year.\n  - The applicant should have a monthly income of ₹15,000/- or below.\n  - The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law.\n  - The applicant should not have membership of the Employees&amp;#39; Provident Fund (EPF)/ National Pension System (NPS)/ Employees&amp;#39; State Insurance Corporation (ESIC).\n  - The applicant should not be an income tax payer.\n\n&gt; ***For the Application of the Welfare Scheme:***\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a registered member under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Punjab.\n  - The applicant should have regularly depositing his contribution.\n  - The scheme applies maximum upto two girls.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/bbgspbocwwb	{"en": "**Financial Assistance:** ₹51,000/- in the form of an Fixed Deposit Receipt (FDR) for each female child (up to two girls).\\n&gt; **Note:** The FDR can only be encashed at the time of the daughter&amp;#39;s marriage.\\n\\n<br>\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:11:02.478+00	t
d50ced20-f634-4092-a9de-6add8e6a7d05	bfa	{"en": "Buti Foundation Award"}	{"en": "The Buti Foundation Award, established in 2007 by the Buti Foundation, New Delhi, is a biennial award recognizing innovative and outstanding research in the field of Plasma Science & Technology. The award aims to honor a Scientist/Engineer under the age of 45 years for their significant contribution"}	Ministry Of Science And Technology	\N	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Scientist/Engineer."}, {"op": "lt", "field": "age", "value": 45}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have conducted innovative and outstanding research in the field of Plasma Science &amp;amp; Technology in India."}]}	\n  - The applicant should be a Scientist/Engineer.\n  - The applicant’s age should be under 45 years as of 1st January 2021 (born on or after 02.01.1976).\n  - The applicant should have conducted innovative and outstanding research in the field of Plasma Science &amp;amp; Technology in India.\n\n<br>\n\n<br>\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/bfa	{"en": "\\n- **Award Amount:** ₹50,000/-- **Award Recognition:** Medal\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:12:43.059+00	t
1fd0aaa7-aae1-4a97-ab87-9385b473c8e5	bnlbks	{"en": "Bebe Nanki Laadli Beti Kalyan Scheme"}	{"en": "Bebe Nanki Laadli Beti Kalyan Scheme was launched under the 13th Finance Commission component for \\"measures to improve gender ratio\\" in the Punjab State from 2011-12. "}	Department of Social Security and Development of Women and Children	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "Abandoned girl children found on or after 1 January 2011 and residing in orphanages or Children’s Homes in Punjab are also eligible."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "The benefit of the scheme is not applicable to newly born male children."}, {"op": "lt", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 30000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Proof of income must be provided in the form of a Blue Card issued by the Food and Supply Department, Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "If the girl child drops out of school for any reason, the benefits under the scheme will be discontinued from that date onward."}]}	\n1. The girl child must have been born on or after 1 January 2011.\n1. The parents of the girl child must be permanent residents of Punjab.\n1. Abandoned girl children found on or after 1 January 2011 and residing in orphanages or Children’s Homes in Punjab are also eligible.\n1. The number of girl children born before this date will not be considered while determining eligibility.\n1. The benefit of the scheme is not applicable to newly born male children.\n1. The annual family income should be less than ₹30,000.\n1. Proof of income must be provided in the form of a Blue Card issued by the Food and Supply Department, Punjab.\n1. If the girl child drops out of school for any reason, the benefits under the scheme will be discontinued from that date onward.\n\n<br>\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/bnlbks	{"en": "**Benefits**\\nFinancial assistance of Rs.61,000 to the Guardian of Girl Child in different stages up to the age of 18 years. \\nS NoPeriod of benefitAgeThe amount released by LIC to the guardian of the beneficiary1On the birth of newly born girl child0 years₹ 2,100/-2On attaining the age of 3 years (after full immunization)3 years₹ 2,100/-3On admission to Class -16 years₹ 2100/-4On admission to Class –IX14 years₹ 2,100/-5On attaining age of 18 years &amp;amp;amp;amp; passed Class- XII18 years₹ 3,1000/-6Scholarship payable-(a)From class-1 to VI standard 100/- per month-₹ 7,200/-(b)From class-VI1 to XII standard 200/- per month-₹ 14,400/-Total benefitAt the age of 18 years₹ 61,000/-<br>\\n\\n<br>\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:10:20.104+00	t
3ea00a24-e1ad-4667-8909-21c3445347a3	btus	{"en": "Bank Tie-Up Scheme"}	{"en": "Through the \\"Bank Tie-Up Scheme\\", the Punjab Scheduled Castes Land Development & Finance Corporation (PSCLDFC) arranges loans through banks, and subsidy is provided by PSCLDFC. The permanent residents of Punjab belonging to Scheduled Castes and living Below Poverty Line are eligible."}	Department of Finance	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a citizen of India."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a domicile / permanent resident of the state of Punjab."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "isBPL", "value": true}, {"op": "in", "field": "category", "values": ["sc"]}, {"op": "eq", "field": "residence", "value": "rural"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not already be availing the benefits of the scheme."}]}	\n1. The applicant should be a citizen of India.\n1. The applicant should be a domicile / permanent resident of the state of Punjab.\n1. The applicant should be from Below Poverty Line (BPL).\n1. The applicant should be from the Scheduled Caste category.\n1. The annual income of the family of the applicant (from all sources) should be ₹ 67,649/- per annum (for rural areas); ₹ 88,756/- per annum (for urban areas).\n1. The applicant should not already be availing the benefits of the scheme.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/btus	\N	\N	2026-09-07 10:10:15.116+00	t
ade01cc6-0562-46e2-89f3-3666bda8935c	csccwpbocwwb	{"en": "Cycle Scheme for the Children of Construction Workers (P.B.O.C.W.W.B)"}	{"en": "The \\"Cycle Scheme for the Children of Construction Workers'' by the BOCW Welfare Board, Department of Labour, Punjab, is a welfare scheme that provides free cycles to the children of registered construction workers once during the period they study in 9th to 12th class in the State of Punjab.\\n"}	Department of Labour	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a resident of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker (Unorganised Worker)."}, {"op": "between", "max": 60, "min": 18, "field": "age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year."}, {"op": "lt", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 15000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not have membership of the Employees&amp;#39; Provident Fund (EPF)/ National Pension System (NPS)/ Employees&amp;#39; State Insurance Corporation (ESIC)."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be an income tax payer."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should be a child of a registered construction worker Under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should be studying in any class between 9th to 12th in the State of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The beneficiary should not have received any bicycle from the State Government under “Mai Bhago Cycle Scheme”."}]}	&gt; ***For Registration as a Building/ Construction Worker:***\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a resident of Punjab.\n  - The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker (Unorganised Worker).\n  - The applicant should be between 18 and 60 years.\n  - The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year.\n  - The applicant should have a monthly income of ₹15,000/- or below.\n  - The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law.\n  - The applicant should not have membership of the Employees&amp;#39; Provident Fund (EPF)/ National Pension System (NPS)/ Employees&amp;#39; State Insurance Corporation (ESIC).\n  - The applicant should not be an income tax payer.\n\n&gt; ***For the Application of the Welfare Scheme:***\n\n\n  - The beneficiary should be a child of a registered construction worker Under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Punjab.\n  - The beneficiary should be studying in any class between 9th to 12th in the State of Punjab.\n  - The beneficiary should not have received any bicycle from the State Government under “Mai Bhago Cycle Scheme”. \n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/csccwpbocwwb	{"en": "\\n- **Quantum of Assistance:** One(1) cycle to the children of registered construction workers.\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:10:43.544+00	t
bc40bf00-2071-49e9-a0a0-16c12de7538f	csspremsobcsi	{"en": "Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Pre-matric Scholarship to Other Backward Classes (OBC) for Studies in India"}	{"en": "\\"Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Pre-matric Scholarship to Other Backward Classes for Studies in India\\" is a Scholarship Scheme by the Ministry of Social Justice and Empowerment. The objective is to award scholarships to school-going children of poorer OBC parents."}	Ministry Of Social Justice and Empowerment	\N	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "lte", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 39}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The scholarship will be tenable only in such institutions and for such pre-matriculation courses, which have been duly recognized by the concerned State Government and Union Territory Administrations."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Regular attendance records of not less than 60% in the previous year should be a pre-requisite for availing scholarship."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The scholar obtaining benefits under this scheme shall not be allowed to avail of benefits under any other pre-matric scholarship scheme."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "gender", "value": "female"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "At least 5% of students with disabilities should be covered by grants or scholarships."}]}	\n1. The scholarship award will be sanctioned in the case of students whose parents/guardians&#39; income from all sources does not exceed ₹ 2,50,000/- per annum.\n1. The scholarship will be tenable only in such institutions and for such pre-matriculation courses, which have been duly recognized by the concerned State Government and Union Territory Administrations.\n1. Regular attendance records of not less than 60% in the previous year should be a pre-requisite for availing scholarship.\n1. The scholar obtaining benefits under this scheme shall not be allowed to avail of benefits under any other pre-matric scholarship scheme.\n\n<br>\n\n**Reservation/ Relaxation/ Preference/ Priority**\n\n1. 30% of the beneficiaries should be reserved for girl students.\n1. At least 5% of students with disabilities should be covered by grants or scholarships.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/csspremsobcsi	{"en": "> **Scholarship**\\n\\n\\n1. Hostellers: Class 3rd to 10th: ₹ 500/- per month for 10 months.\\n1. Day Scholars: Class 1st to 10th: ₹ 100/- per month for 10 months.\\n\\n> **Ad-Hoc Grant**\\n\\n\\n1. An ad-hoc grant of ₹ 500/- per student per annum to all students i.e. hostlers as well as day scholars will also be given.\\n\\n<br>\\n\\nThe scholarship amount will be payable from the date of joining to the date of leaving the school, excluding the period of vacation, which will be about 10 months in a year except in the cases where the students enter late or leave early in the midst of academic year.\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:48:41.669+00	t
335c65a9-98dd-4694-bb74-086e969f8dd8	cvcis	{"en": "Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) Internship Scheme"}	{"en": "CVC initiated an Internship Scheme in the year 2016. This Scheme seeks to engage Indian Nationals, who are Graduates (awaiting final year results) /Post Graduate or Research Students enrolled in reputed Universities/Institutions in India or abroad."}	Ministry Of Personnel, Public Grievances And Pensions	\N	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a citizen of India."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Graduate (awaiting final year results) /Post Graduate or Research Student enrolled in reputed Universities/Institutions within India or abroad and preferably studying Law, IT, MBA, Social Sciences and associated subjects."}]}	\n1. The applicant should be a citizen of India.\n1. The applicant should be a Graduate (awaiting final year results) /Post Graduate or Research Student enrolled in reputed Universities/Institutions within India or abroad and preferably studying Law, IT, MBA, Social Sciences and associated subjects.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/cvcis	{"en": "> **Remuneration**\\n\\nInterns may be given a stipend of ₹ 10,000 per month necessary to meet the conveyance and other daily needs of the Interns. \\n**NOTE:** The internship is neither a job nor a promise for a job in the future.\\n<br>\\n\\n> **Logistics and Support**\\n\\nThe commission shall provide them with working space, internet facility and other necessities as deemed fit by the Branch heads. \\n**NOTE:** The Interns may arrange their own transport and accommodation at their own expense.\\n<br>\\n\\n> **Certificate of Internship**\\n\\nA certificate will be awarded to the Interns upon satisfactory completion of the internship and submission of their end-of-assignment report which will be evaluated by the Branch Officer with whom the intern is attached.\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 09:47:41.819+00	t
13da8e17-dada-441c-adaa-9c441fd9da60	dls-punjab	{"en": "Direct Lending Scheme"}	{"en": "Through the \\"Direct Lending Scheme\\", the Punjab Scheduled Castes Land Development & Finance Corporation (PSCLDFC) provides direct loans for the economic upliftment of the members of the Scheduled Castes and Handicapped People in the state of Punjab."}	Department of Finance	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a citizen of India."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a domicile / permanent resident of the state of Punjab."}, {"op": "eq", "field": "isBPL", "value": true}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "The applicant should be from the Scheduled Caste category OR the applicant should be a Person with Disability (PwD)"}, {"op": "between", "max": 55, "min": 18, "field": "age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "ambiguous", "sourceText": "(At the time of considering the loan case of the applicant) The annual family income of the applicant (from all sources) should be less than or equal to ₹ 1,00,000/- (In case the applicant is unemployed, and intends to start his/her own business, his/her family income may not be taken into consideration)."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not already be availing the benefits of the scheme."}]}	\n1. The applicant should be a citizen of India.\n1. The applicant should be a domicile / permanent resident of the state of Punjab.\n1. The applicant should be from Below Poverty Line (BPL).\n1. The applicant should be from the Scheduled Caste category OR the applicant should be a Person with Disability (PwD)\n1. The age of the applicant should be between 18 to 55 years.\n1. (At the time of considering the loan case of the applicant) The annual family income of the applicant (from all sources) should be less than or equal to ₹ 1,00,000/- (In case the applicant is unemployed, and intends to start his/her own business, his/her family income may not be taken into consideration).\n1. The applicant should not already be availing the benefits of the scheme.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/dls-punjab	\N	\N	2026-09-07 10:10:12.193+00	t
aa08cb52-b8b6-4d35-b457-763a4dd8200f	dpps	{"en": "Disabled Person Pension Scheme - Punjab"}	{"en": "Punjab State Government started a pension for disable person of the state. "}	Department of Social Security and Development of Women and Children	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Applicant should be a Permanent Resident of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "Applicant should be Disabled and the Disability Percentage should be more than 50%."}, {"op": "lte", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 60000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "People with mental disabilities are eligible regardless of their specific disability."}]}	\n1. Applicant should be a Permanent Resident of Punjab.\n1. Applicant should be Disabled and the Disability Percentage should be more than 50%.\n1. The Annual Income of Family should not be more than Rs. 60,000/- per Year.\n1. People with mental disabilities are eligible regardless of their specific disability.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/dpps	{"en": "Amount : ₹ 1,500/- per month\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:09:43.293+00	t
a94984b8-63c3-4dd5-a8b1-21825c68655b	dshaspbocwwb	{"en": "Denture, Spectacles & Hearing Aid Scheme (P.B.O.C.W.W.B)"}	{"en": "The \\"Denture, Spectacles & Hearing Aid Scheme'' by the BOCW Welfare Board, Department of Labour, Punjab, is a welfare scheme that provides financial aid to beneficiary construction workers & their families for denture, spectacles & hearing aid.\\n"}	Department of Labour	PB	{"op": "AND", "clauses": [{"op": "in", "field": "state", "values": ["PB"]}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a resident of Punjab."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker (Unorganised Worker)."}, {"op": "between", "max": 60, "min": 18, "field": "age"}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year."}, {"op": "lt", "field": "annualIncome", "value": 15000}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not have membership of the Employees&amp;#39; Provident Fund (EPF)/ National Pension System (NPS)/ Employees&amp;#39; State Insurance Corporation (ESIC)."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should not be an income tax payer."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be a registered member Under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Punjab or should be a family member of the worker."}, {"op": "WILDCARD", "reason": "unmodellable", "sourceText": "The applicant should be paying the contribution regularly."}]}	&gt; ***For Registration as a Building/ Construction Worker:***\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a resident of Punjab.\n  - The applicant should be a Building/ Construction Worker (Unorganised Worker).\n  - The applicant should be between 18 and 60 years.\n  - The applicant should have engaged in building and construction work for at least 90 days in a given year.\n  - The applicant should have a monthly income of ₹15,000/- or below.\n  - The applicant should not be a member of any other Welfare Fund established under any law.\n  - The applicant should not have membership of the Employees&amp;#39; Provident Fund (EPF)/ National Pension System (NPS)/ Employees&amp;#39; State Insurance Corporation (ESIC).\n  - The applicant should not be an income tax payer.\n\n&gt; ***For the Application of the Welfare Scheme:***\n\n\n  - The applicant should be a registered member Under the Building and Other Construction Workers Welfare Board of Punjab or should be a family member of the worker.\n  - The applicant should be paying the contribution regularly.\n\n	https://www.myscheme.gov.in/schemes/dshaspbocwwb	{"en": "\\n- **Spectacle:** ₹.800/-.- **Denture:** ₹5,000/-.- **Hearing Aid:** ₹6,000/-.\\n&gt; **Note:**\\n\\n\\n  - Financial assistance under this scheme shall be granted on the recommendation of Govt. medical officer/Incharge of the E.S.I Dispensary.\\n  - Under this scheme, the beneficiary or his family members shall get benefit only once.\\n  - The beneficiary shall get the amount of actual expenditure or amount of financial assistance, whichever is less, on the basis of actual bills produced by him.\\n\\n"}	\N	2026-09-07 10:10:45.457+00	t
